{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":"/jbTqU6BJMufoMnPSlO4ThrcXs3Y.jpg","created_by":[{"id":52139,"credit_id":"5256e93919c2956ff610860e","name":"Seth MacFarlane","original_name":"Seth MacFarlane","gender":2,"profile_path":"/8oQJqM51Z0Qtdb7sE6ZfX1peNCB.jpg"}],"episode_run_time":[],"first_air_date":"1999-01-31","genres":[{"id":16,"name":"Animation"},{"id":35,"name":"Comedy"}],"homepage":"https://www.fox.com/detail/series/SER000854XOPZ/family-guy","id":1434,"in_production":true,"languages":["en"],"last_air_date":"2026-05-17","last_episode_to_air":{"id":7193771,"name":"High School History","overview":"In this three-act parody of prominent historical eras, the Griffins take a humorous look at The French Revolution, the American Civil War, and World War II.","vote_average":6.5,"vote_count":2,"air_date":"2026-05-17","episode_number":15,"episode_type":"finale","production_code":"RACX09","runtime":30,"season_number":24,"show_id":1434,"still_path":"/8cZI6xE1kZWIB8JOTtaVKTbDtD7.jpg"},"name":"Family Guy","next_episode_to_air":null,"networks":[{"id":19,"logo_path":"/1DSpHrWyOORkL9N2QHX7Adt31mQ.png","name":"FOX","origin_country":"US"}],"number_of_episodes":456,"number_of_seasons":24,"origin_country":["US"],"original_language":"en","original_name":"Family Guy","overview":"Sick, twisted, politically incorrect and Freakin' Sweet animated series featuring the adventures of the dysfunctional Griffin family. Bumbling Peter and long-suffering Lois have three kids. Stewie (a brilliant but sadistic baby bent on killing his mother and taking over the world), Meg (the oldest, and is the most unpopular girl in town) and Chris (the middle kid, he's not very bright but has a passion for movies). The final member of the family is Brian - a talking dog and much more than a pet, he keeps Stewie in check whilst sipping Martinis and sorting through his own life issues.","popularity":313.2007,"poster_path":"/3PFsEuAiyLkWsP4GG6dIV37Q6gu.jpg","production_companies":[{"id":1556,"logo_path":"/31h94rG9hzjprXoYNy3L1ErUya2.png","name":"20th Century Fox Television","origin_country":"US"},{"id":8789,"logo_path":"/1smGq637YoNgkeBZXt7TAPDYGda.png","name":"Fuzzy Door Productions","origin_country":"US"},{"id":154887,"logo_path":"/wLFPu95hIMmyLR5hdtvYaMuK0tG.png","name":"20th Television Animation","origin_country":"US"},{"id":236166,"logo_path":"/8rFlu5iytnjsciYXZDw90ktllCI.png","name":"20th Television","origin_country":"US"}],"production_countries":[{"iso_3166_1":"US","name":"United States of America"}],"seasons":[{"air_date":"1995-01-01","episode_count":27,"id":3831,"name":"Specials","overview":"Special installments of the series.","poster_path":"/4RkfMO31xiXMIiMc0BtU4fKhOKr.jpg","season_number":0,"vote_average":0},{"air_date":"1999-01-31","episode_count":7,"id":3821,"name":"Season 1","overview":"Meet the Griffins: Peter, the big loveable oaf who always says what's on his mind. Lois, the doting mother who can't figure out why her baby son keeps trying to kill her. Their daughter Meg, the teen drama queen who's constantly embarrassed by her family. Chris, the beefy 13-year-old who wouldn't hurt a fly, unless it landed on his hot dog. Stewie, the maniacal one-year-old bent on world domination. And Brian, the sarcastic dog with a wit as dry as the martinis he drinks. The animated adventures of this outrageous family will have your whole family laughing out loud.","poster_path":"/ob5IdvZFQu5XBUkH6OzTc1A5fjV.jpg","season_number":1,"vote_average":7.2},{"air_date":"1999-09-23","episode_count":21,"id":3822,"name":"Season 2","overview":"","poster_path":"/pvbIKvlRQaxOqgAudkh6avAMKoS.jpg","season_number":2,"vote_average":7.3},{"air_date":"2001-07-11","episode_count":22,"id":3823,"name":"Season 3","overview":"In this hilarious third season, the Griffin family faces all-new dilemmas, including Brian's unintentional foray into directing porn, Stewie's rants on national TV, Meg's date with a nudist and Lois' Yuletide insanity. Meanwhile, Peter is surprised to discover Lois was once a groupie, and his son, Chris, is more \"endowed\" than he is.","poster_path":"/iFmuPeKkezeYbzZnDf2DbFPqwOc.jpg","season_number":3,"vote_average":7},{"air_date":"2005-05-01","episode_count":30,"id":3824,"name":"Season 4","overview":"The wildly irreverent, shrewdly crude animated sensation that has been confounding the PC police since the last millennium is back! Not even the insufferable humiliation of network cancellation was enough to keep \"TV's most outrageous cartoon clan\" down. So raise your martini glasses in unison as \"Family Guy\" returns with a vengeance for more hilarious episodes that find Peter going blind, Lois in prison, Meg getting a makeover, Chris befriending a talking zit, Stewie smitten with his sitter, and Brian winning the heart of \"The Bachelorette\".","poster_path":"/s3gDwVzT8X4LHwZbXeKU7xm5oMo.jpg","season_number":4,"vote_average":7},{"air_date":"2006-09-10","episode_count":18,"id":3825,"name":"Season 5","overview":"The hilarity continues this season when Brian and Stewie hit the road in search of Rupert, Stewie's teddy bear, after he's accidentally sold at a garage sale.","poster_path":"/vb1OIK6wOU8MNzNOTbgNy5qMek6.jpg","season_number":5,"vote_average":7},{"air_date":"2007-09-23","episode_count":12,"id":3826,"name":"Season 6","overview":"","poster_path":"/A015AO0mBU0IjGO7HbBYwV115nJ.jpg","season_number":6,"vote_average":7.1},{"air_date":"2008-09-28","episode_count":16,"id":3827,"name":"Season 7","overview":"","poster_path":"/hiNM0FdEGu6uxJHDSZ8tX8Dck5o.jpg","season_number":7,"vote_average":7},{"air_date":"2009-09-26","episode_count":20,"id":3828,"name":"Season 8","overview":"Stewie and Brian travel through alternate universes in an homage to \"Sliders,\" spies Dan Aykroyd and Chevy Chase (guest-voicing as themselves) move into Cleveland's old house and Stewie scores tickets to a Hannah Montana concert.","poster_path":"/htOnnZJpAic9ZFbYTxSgska6bDt.jpg","season_number":8,"vote_average":6.8},{"air_date":"2010-09-26","episode_count":18,"id":3829,"name